course: dictionary
lesson: 13269
title: The golfer
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A golfer is a person who plays golf. In golf, you hit a small ball with a club and try to get it into a hole, using as few hits as possible. «My uncle is a keen golfer, so he plays every Saturday.» Keen means he likes it a lot, and the word golfer tells you he plays golf.
explain: Look at the clues around the word. «The professional golfer hit the ball into the hole in just three strokes.» Professional means she plays golf as her job. A stroke is one hit of the ball, so three strokes means three hits. The fewer strokes, the better.
explain: Check your meaning by putting it into the sentence. Try «The person who plays golf hit the ball into the hole in just three strokes.» It still makes sense, so golfer means a person who plays golf.
fact: A golfer is a person who plays golf.
fact: In golf, you hit a small ball with a club and try to get it into a hole.
fact: A stroke is one hit of the ball. The golfer who uses the fewest strokes usually wins.
fact: A golf course in these lessons has 18 holes.
fact: Par is the number of strokes expected for a hole. Scores below par are shown with a minus sign, like -2, and scores above par are shown with a plus sign, like +3.
exercise: «My dad is a keen golfer, so he plays on Saturdays.» What is a golfer? | *A person who plays golf | A type of golf club | A small ball used in tennis | A golf course with 18 holes
exercise: In golf, what does a golfer try to do with the number of hits? | *Use as few hits as possible | Hit the ball as far as possible | Hit the ball as many times as possible | Stop playing at once
exercise: Find and copy one word that means a person who plays golf. | course | hole | golf | *golfer
test: «The professional golfer hit the ball into the hole in just three strokes.» What is a stroke in golf? | A kind of golf club | A hole in the grass | *One hit of the ball | A walk around the course
test: Sam walked round a golf course with 18 holes. How many holes was that? | Eight | *Eighteen | Twenty | Nine
exam: Mia's golf scores were -2, +3 and +1. Which score is the best, because the lowest score wins? | +1 | +3 | *-2
</br>
